OscillatoryPeriodOfAMassOfASpring

The Oscillatory Period of a Mass on a Spring

An undamped spring-mass system undergoes simple harmonic motion. Its oscillatory period is dependent on the mass of the object and the spring constant of the spring.

T = 2 \pi \sqrt{\frac{m}{k}}

where:

T [var. scal. Period] is the period of oscillation
m [var. scal. Mass] is the mass
k [var. scal. SpringConstant] is the spring constant

